        "severity": "low",
        "category": "error-handling",
        "title": "DNS GC permanently disabled if endpoint restore wait fails",
        "explanation": "bootstrapCompleted is only set when waitForEndpointRestore succeeds. If RestorerPromise.Await or WaitForEndpointRestore returns an error, the flag stays false, and every later doGC run returns early. DNS caches then never expire and stale ipcache metadata is never removed, so memory and ipcache entries grow without bound. The only sign is a Debug log line. Before this change, GC ran either way.",
        "suggestion": "Make sure the gate is eventually lifted, for example by setting bootstrapCompleted on the error path or after a timeout. Alternatively, log a warning or update health status when GC has been skipped for too long.",
        "evidence": "if !n.hasBootstrapCompleted() {",
